-- title:
--   Quadratic word budget for the complete local-cover setup
-- statement:
--   Let $h,B\in\mathbb N$, and write $L=512h$. In the concrete local-cover construction, let $v$ be the number of enumerated vertices, $p$ its selected prime, $c$ its bucket cap, $R$ the number of candidate weight assignments, and $T$ the schedule length. Assume $B\ge1$ and that each of
--   $L+1$, $v+1$, $p+1$, $c+1$, $R+1$, $T+1$, $p^{2L+1}+1$, and $2^{L+1}+1$ is at most $B$. If $W_{\mathrm{setup}}(h)$ denotes the setup procedure's integer-magnitude budget, then
--
--   $$
--   W_{\mathrm{setup}}(h)\le 2000B^2.
--   $$
--
--   These are precisely the common dimension bounds packaged by the local-cover resource interface. The conclusion provides one word-value budget for coefficient decoding, histograms, pair flags, cover construction, and gathering selected rows.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverResources.lean#L38-L88

